# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVACY BOUNDARY — read before editing.
#
# This is a PUBLIC repository. It must never contain real information about
# any section member: no names, phone numbers, emails, photos, birthdays.
#
# All real data lives in the separate PRIVATE repo (section-j-data) and is
# pulled in only by CI at deploy time. Locally it is expected at
# ../section-j-data, which is outside this repo entirely.
#
# The rules below are belt-and-braces in case someone copies real data in here
# by accident. `npm run check:leaks` is the actual enforcement — run it before
# you push, and CI runs it on every pull request.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Real roster data, in every spelling someone might reach for
data/private/
data/raw/
data/roster.json
data/meetup-history.json
data/overrides.json
data/*.csv
data/photos/
**/classcards-export*
**/ClasscardsDownload*

# Build-time encrypted payloads (regenerated by CI; never committed)
public/data/*.enc
public/data/manifest.json

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Cloudflare Wrangler's local-secrets file for `wrangler pages dev` —
# ADMIN_PASSPHRASE_HASH / ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET / GITHUB_ADMIN_TOKEN for local
# testing only. Real values live in the Cloudflare dashboard, never here.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.wrangler/

# Local machine and employer specifics. Claude reads this alongside CLAUDE.md,
# but it must never ship to the section in a public repo.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Node / build
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# Editors & OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log
